# malosound — what git tracks, and what it must never touch.
#
# The one rule this file exists to enforce: AUDIO BYTES NEVER GO IN GIT.
# This repo holds code and configuration. The bytes live in the library
# (see LIBRARY_PATH.md). The repo references the library; the library holds it.
#
# TWO THINGS GIT CANNOT PROTECT. Do not assume a rule below covers them:
#   projects/          — ignored wholesale, by design. Live sets never enter git.
#   Samples/Imported/  — only ever exists INSIDE a Live project, therefore inside
#                        the ignore above. It is NOT regenerable, and no
#                        .gitignore rule can save it. docs/BACKUP.md is what
#                        protects it. (A `Samples/Processed/` rule used to sit
#                        here looking reassuring and doing nothing. It is gone.)

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Live sets
# Binary, churns on every save, drags gigabytes of samples behind it.
projects/
Backup/
*.als.bak
Ableton Project Info/
*.asd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- audio
# There are NO negations below this block. If you want one, the answer is
# docs/BACKUP.md or a pointer in the release metadata — not git.
*.wav
*.aif
*.aiff
*.flac
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.wv
*.rex
*.rx2
bounces/
renders/
releases/**/masters/
releases/**/audio/

# ------------------------------------------------------- Max for Live devices
# Source of truth is the UNFROZEN devices/<Name>/src/*.maxpat — text, diffable,
# reviewable, committed. The ONLY .amxd git accepts is a FROZEN export sitting
# in devices/<Name>/dist/. Freezing embeds the dependencies; an unfrozen device
# that leaves this machine is a device that will not open. .githooks/pre-commit
# enforces both halves — read it before you fight it.
*.amxd
!devices/*/dist/*.amxd
*.maxpat.bak
*.maxhelp
Max Autosave/
*.maxsnap
devices/**/externals/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- build
artifacts/
build/
_to_delete/
_stale-locks-*/
cmake-build*/
*.o
*.obj
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.vst3
*.component

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------- junk
# The Ableton plan targets a MacBook + PC rig, so both dialects of noise land here.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
